## 3.12 Validation Reference

### Purpose

The Validation Reference section identifies the approved validation approach and associated engineering artifacts used to demonstrate that a System Objective fulfills its intended engineering need.

Its purpose is to establish a consistent link between the objective and its validation evidence without embedding detailed validation procedures.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective shall include the following fields:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Validation Method | Approved method used to validate the objective. |
| Validation Reference | Reference to the governing validation document or plan. |
| Validation Criteria | High-level criteria defining successful validation. |
| Validation Status | Current validation state of the objective. |
| Validation Evidence | Reference to the evidence produced during validation, where applicable. |

---

### Validation Rules

Validation information shall:

- Reference approved validation artifacts.
- Remain consistent with the Objective Governance framework.
- Be updated as validation activities progress.
- Preserve links to all validation evidence.
- Demonstrate that the objective satisfies the intended engineering purpose.

---

### Engineering Note

Validation confirms that achieving the objective delivers the intended value within the system context.

Detailed validation procedures, operational assessments, and acceptance records shall be maintained in dedicated validation documents rather than within the objective itself.
